Z||000044||Monkeyman||12-27-1999||12:59 AM||||The Pantera was a car made by DeTomaso.  The hotrod version (with all the cool body work) was the Pantera GT5.  (Note--That's "5", not "S".)  The only motor available in the Pantera was the Ford 351.  Any other motors in that car were aftermarket/somebody elses.  The body was cool.  The interior was very '70s.  Makes the Fiero interior look like the Jetsons. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/'87_Pantera.jpg"> This is an '87 Pantera GT5<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pantera-interior.jpg"> And this is the interior||||reg||1
Z||000045||XenoGen||12-27-1999||10:01 AM||||That's a pretty neat car, the Pantera GT5. Would that be something like a precursor to the Ford GT40 and GT90? Did the Pantera go into mass production, or were there only a small number of the cars?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000046||Monkeyman||12-27-1999||01:30 PM||||The Ford GT40 was the late '60s, I think.  I don't know about the other.  DeTomaso only made a couple thousand of the Panteras and only a handful of them had the GT5 package.  There were 3 GT5i cars built with a specially tuned 351, slightly wider wheels (like 12" wide back wheels aren't wide enough!), and even more agressive body work.  Jay Leno owns one, one was destroyed, and the other has something like 3 miles on it.  Supposedly that one is sitting in the companys' warehouse under wraps.  The Pantera is supposed to be a world class car (at least from the standards when they were built), but the interior is just too generic.<BR>  I still like the Fiero better.  The Pantera is too big.  Long live the Fiero!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000047||fiero56||12-28-1999||10:11 PM||||Monkeyman,<BR>You have all the picutes. At first I figured you had saved all these Fiero pictures. Now your posting the Pantera, and I'm willing to bet you have a ton more just waiting to be posted when the time arrives.||||reg||14
